  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resiliency in Northern Ghana II - Systems Strengthening (Technical Assistance)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Ghana):  This activity aims to improve household nutrition and resilience within the 17 target Feed the Future zone of influence districts in northern Ghana by strengthening the capacity of public and private institutions to plan, finance, and implement solutions to malnutrition and food insecurity. With FY 2022 funds, the activity will identify and partner with strategic local partners through sub-grants and technical capacity building to promote positive nutrition behaviors and build household resilience in these communities. Contributing to reaching global targets of the USAID Multi-sectoral Nutrition Strategy, the activity will promote evidence-based practices, including exclusive breastfeeding; appropriate complementary feeding; dietary diversity, particularly for pregnant and lactating women; community identification and treatment of acute malnutrition; improved sanitary practices; uptake of family planning services; prevention and treatment of infections; income generating activities; and gender equity. It will also advance a local solutions approach by strengthening operations and administration of three local partner institutions in order to transition to direct awards from USAID in Year 4. Building on previous USG investments in local governance strengthening, the activity will enhance local governments&apos; systems to improve functions such as public financial management; planning across sectors; revenue generation; and use of data for planning and decision-making. It will also work with the districts to increase the quality and efficiency of social services critical to building resilience, such as the national cash transfer program, the school feeding program, and the National Health Insurance Scheme.</narrative>
  </description>
